AD  - Electric Power University, Faculty of Electronics & Telecom, Hanoi, Viet Nam
AB  - This paper proposes a lightweight authentication protocol designed for resource-constrained embedded systems deployed on unmanned aerial vehicles (UAVs). The protocol leverages the structure of a nonlinear pseudo-random sequence to enhance security while maintaining low computational complexity. The randomness and linear complexity of the protocol are evaluated using the NIST statistical test suite. The protocol is simulated on an ESP32 microcontroller connected to an SX1278 LoRa module to assess its feasibility and system response time. Experimental results show that the random sequence used in the protocol passes seven fundamental NIST tests. When implemented on the microcontroller, the proposed protocol occupies 24% of the Flash memory, 22% of the RAM, and requires 650 ms for authentication. These results demonstrate the practicality of applying the proposed protocol in real-world scenarios.  © 2025 IEEE.
