AB  - Internet of Things (IoT) technology is one of the supporters of Industry 4.0 which requires a minimum of human error and runs 24/7 so that easier to manage and more accurate without human intervention. One of the current trending IoT communication modules is the Long Range (LoRa). LoRa has the advantage of long communication distances and energy-saving modules. However, LoRa also has a drawback where it transmits data via radio waves so that other LoRa with the same frequency can receive the data even though they are not legitimate recipients. Therefore, this study implements the MICKEY cipher algorithm to secure data to maintain data confidentiality based on LoRa communication. The result of this research is the confidentiality of data transmission between LoRa is guaranteed from eavesdroppers or other unauthorized recipients. The evaluation of security is considered effective and capable of securing data effectively, as demonstrated by the evidence from passive and active attack i.e., sniffing and Known Plaintext Attack (KPA). © 2023 ACM.
