TI  - Lightweight Ensemble Deep Learning-Based Device Identification for LoRa RF Fingerprinting in IoT Networks
ST  - IoT Aglari için Hafif Ensemble Derin Ögrenme ile LoRa RF Fingerprinting Temelli Cihaz Tanima
PY  - 2026
T2  - SIU 2026 - 34th Signal Processing and Communications Applications Conference, Conference Proceedings
DO  - 10.1109/SIU71813.2026.11636870
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105048641197?origin=resultslist
AD  - İzmir Bakirçay Üniversitesi, Elektrik-Elektronik Mühendisliǧi Bölümü, İzmir, Turkey
AB  - Device authentication in LoRa-based IoT networks has become an important research topic, particularly from the perspective of physical-layer security. In this study, a lightweight and effective RF fingerprinting approach is proposed to identify LoRa devices by exploiting hardware-specific signal characteristics. The proposed method relies on a soft voting-based ensemble classification strategy to combine complementary features learned by different architectures. Specifically, ChirpNet-Lite, which models the time-frequency structure of LoRa signals, and Extreme-Lite, which provides a low parameter count and fast inference, are jointly employed. The class probabilities produced by these two models are combined through a soft voting mechanism to obtain a more robust classification. The proposed method is evaluated on the official test split of the LoRa_RFFI dataset. Experimental results show that the method achieves an accuracy of 98.90%, demonstrating competitive performance compared to many existing approaches in literature. Furthermore, the model contains only approximately 57 K parameters and 15.37M FLOPs, highlighting its computational efficiency. This makes the proposed approach particularly suitable for deployment on resource-constrained IoT gateways and edge systems. © 2026 IEEE.
