AD  - Bppimt, Department of Information Technology, Kolkata, India
AD  - Hit, Department of CSE(AI & ML), Haldia, India
AB  - The growing adoption of of Internet of Things (IoT) devices necessitates secure and energy-efficient communication protocols to address the constraints of limited computational resources and power consumption. While the Message Queuing Telemetry Transport (MQTT) protocol is widely adopted for IoT messaging, its reliance on Transport Layer Security (TLS) introduces significant overhead, making it unsuitable for resource-constrained devices. Compared to traditional AES-128-GCM implementations, ASCON-MQTT achieves significantly improved performance metrics, demonstrating 1.4 times faster than AES-based and 4 times fastert than TLS on ESP32 platforms. By replacing the computational overhead of AES and TLS with ASCON's lightweight authenticated encryption, our solution simultaneously enhances both security and efficiency. This paper presents ASCON-MQTT, a lightweight framework that integrates the NIST-standardized ASCON cryptographic algorithm with MQTT to provide end-to-end security while optimizing energy efficiency. ASCON-MQTT ensures confidentiality, integrity, and authenticity at the application layer, eliminating the need for a trusted broker. Our results show that ASCON-MQTT is a viable solution for secure and sustainable IoT deployments in smart cities, industrial automation, and healthcare monitoring systems. © 2025 IEEE.
