AB  - This paper presents a secure and energy-efficient LoRa communication framework that integrates AES-GCM encryption and Elliptic Curve Cryptography (ECC) key exchange for robust protection against replay and MITM attacks. The system, implemented on ESP32 with a TFT-based monitoring interface and renewable energy integration, addresses the challenges of secure communication in disaster-prone and resource-constrained IoT deployments. Real-world experiments demonstrate up to 96% packet delivery ratio, reduced latency (120-150 ms), and 15-20% lower power consumption compared to baseline LoRa setups, with reliable communication maintained up to 1500 m. The proposed system balances long-range connectivity, strong security, and low-power operation, offering a practical solution for future IoT applications. © 2025 IEEE.
