AB  - This study presents the design and simulation of a lightweight cryptographic protocol for smart home IoT devices using ChaCha20 and Ascon-AEAD128. The protocol was implemented in Python and tested in a virtual ESP32 environment using Wokwi and CloudAMQP. It ensures both confidentiality and integrity by combining stream cipher encryption with authenticated message tagging. Two transmission scenarios, normal and tampered, were evaluated to verify tag validation and message decryption. Results confirmed that the system reliably detects tampering and prevents unauthorized decryption. The study highlights the practicality of modern AEAD ciphers for constrained devices and offers a complete, testable protocol for secure IoT communication. This implementation contributes a functional, scalable solution aligned with NIST cryptographic standards for low-power IoT networks. ©2025 IEEE.
