AB  - Post-quantum cryptography represents one of the most promising areas of modern cryptography. The development in this discipline significantly accelerated after it became of interest to the National Institute of Standards and Technology (NIST). One of the important research directions in this area is the practical deployment of post-quantum cryptographic algorithms on resource-constrained devices. In this article, we investigate the possibility of deploying post-quantum cryptography on small processors with limited random access memory (RAM) capacity. These processors are commonly used in Internet of Things (IoT) devices, where the practical deployment of post-quantum algorithms remains challenging due to computational and memory constraints. We select a suitable algorithm and perform several implementation modifications that enable its execution on microcontrollers with limited memory resources. © 2026 by the authors.
