AB  - The rapid growth of Internet of Things (IoT) technologies has created significant security challenges due to the limited computational and memory resources of embedded devices. Traditional encryption schemes often impose high computational overhead, making them unsuitable for resource-constrained environments. This paper presents the development of a modified homomorphic encryption scheme for ESP32-based IoT devices. The proposed scheme enables secure data encryption and decryption while supporting limited processing on encrypted data. The algorithm was implemented on the ESP32 microcontroller, and its performance was evaluated in terms of execution time and memory consumption. Experimental results demonstrate that the modified scheme reduces computational overhead while maintaining an adequate level of security, confirming the feasibility of using homomorphic encryption in resource-constrained IoT devices for secure data processing.  © 2026 IEEE.
