AB  - Blockchain and InterPlanetary File System (IPFS) have been widely adopted to ensure model integrity in federated learning. Although some studies have implemented federated learning clients on resource-constrained Internet of Things (IoT) devices, none have integrated cryptographic algorithms alongside blockchain and IPFS on such devices. This paper addresses this gap by introducing a lightweight symmetric encryption protocol to protect the confidentiality of on-chain IPFS content identifiers (CIDs), preventing unauthorized access to model updates while still leveraging IPFS and blockchain for integrity verification. A proof-of-concept is conducted on the ESP32-C6-DevKitC-1 to demonstrate its practical feasibility. The proposed solution demonstrates efficient resource utilization, requiring only 1.08 MB of flash memory, 42.80 KB of RAM, and achieving a computation time of 12.51 seconds. The proposed protocol is formally analyzed using ProVerif and shown to be secure against three common IoT attacks: key disclosure, replay, and adversarial-in-the-middle attacks. These results highlight the potential to deploy secure federated learning on resource-limited embedded platforms by seamlessly integrating blockchain, IPFS, and lightweight symmetric cryptography.  © 2026 IEEE.
