AB  - Post-Quantum Cryptography (PQC) is essential to secure future Internet-of-Things (IoT) systems against quantum adversaries. CRYSTALS-Kyber, recently standardized by NIST, provides efficient key encapsulation for constrained devices. This paper investigates Kyber's interoperability across heterogeneous IoT platforms - Raspberry Pi, ESP32, and x86-64 laptops - using the MQTT protocol. We demonstrate successful key exchanges among homogeneous platforms and mixed Raspberry Pi-laptop systems, but observe failures in ESP32 cross-platform exchanges. Analysis indicates that inconsistent shared secrets originate from entropy variations in platform-specific Random Number Generators (RNGs). Our results highlight the need for standardized entropy handling in PQC implementations for seamless IoT integration. © 2026 IEEE.
