AB  - The proceedings contain 34 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Electronics, Communications and Control Engineering. The topics include: Design and Synthesis of Capacitance Multiplier Using LT1228s and a Grounded Capacitor; a Reliability and Performance Study of Neural Networks on Resource-Constrained Platforms; binary Splitting Test Generation for a Pattern Matching Accelerator with In-Memory-Processing Architecture; 650 V Multiple Floating P Oxide-Trenches High-Conductivity Insulated Gate Bipolar Transistor Design; A Low-Power and Small-Area Squarer for Wearable ECG Devices Utilizing Pan-Tompkins Algorithm; reliability Calculation for Paper Robots, Case Study: Assistive Robot with Human; analysis and Experiment of a Three-Phase Hybrid Fibonacci-Type Marx Generator; low-Cost Smartphone-Controlled Exercise Machine for Arm and Leg Muscles; assessing the Impact of Oil Type on Transformer Performance and Mass; a New Design Methodology for Aircraft Data Logger Adopting Pulse-Mode Circuit Approach; impact of Altitude on the Design and Performance of Dry-Type Transformers; ioT System for Access and Control with Integrated Lighting: Case Study and Reliability; optimizing Power Efficiency in Cloud Environments for Carrier-Grade Applications; a Review of Machine Learning-Based Security Algorithms for the Internet of Things; Potential of TinyML and Federated Reinforcement Learning-Based Trajectory Optimization in Space-Air-Ground Integrated Network; water Quality Monitoring and Control System for Tilapia Fingerling Rearing; Implementation of the 5G Software Defined Radio via FPGA; Reliability of IoT Ambient Lighting Based on NodeMCU and RGB Color Sensors; enhanced Lightweight Cryptography Security Algorithm for the Internet of Things; application of LoRa Technology in a Hydroponic System to Improve Lettuce Cultivation in Urban Areas.
