AD  - Department of Computer Science and Engineering, Indian Institute of Technology Jammu, Jammu, 181221, India
AD  - Department of Electrical Engineering, Indian Institute of Technology Jammu, Jammu, 181221, India
AB  - Internet of Things (IoT) deployments comprise large numbers of resource-constrained devices operating in physically exposed environments, where secure key storage and long-term secret management remain challenging. Existing authentication schemes often incur high computational and communication overheads, while conventional logic locking techniques primarily focus on intellectual property protection without addressing device authentication or secure communication. This work presents a unified framework that integrates SRAM Physical Unclonable Function (PUF)-based logic locking to enable lightweight authentication, key establishment and IP protection. The proposed authentication protocol relies exclusively on hash and masking operations, avoiding expensive cryptographic operations, and key storage. Formal security verification using the Verifpal tool and ROR-Oracle model confirms resistance against replay, impersonation, and man-in-the-middle attacks, while guaranteeing authentication and confidentiality properties. Compared to state-of-the-art schemes, the proposed protocol achieves the lowest computational and communication overhead, completing authentication with a total transmission cost of 1096 bits, while also minimizing computation overhead by relying on a reduced set of lightweight cryptographic operations. Analysis of ten ESP32 devices implementing SRAM-PUFs shows resilience against modeling attacks using classical and deep learning models, including Logistic Regression, SVM, Random Forest, kNN, MLP, LSTM, and Transformer architectures. Moreover, experimental results across ten ESP32 devices show strong intra-device reliability exceeding 96 percent and near-ideal inter-device uniqueness, validating the applicability of the proposed solution in real-world IoT environments. © 2026 Elsevier Ltd.
